    "title": "KoalaBear m2 r4 coordinate negative one-loop 442 S1 forced-loop deployed product exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "raw unit-ideal deletion of both forced-loop S1 cells in the representative common sign row",
    "statement": "In common sign row (1,1), force the S1 loop product -d^2=m. The element -m is a nonsquare in each cubic common component, so adjoining theta with theta^2=-m gives two genuine degree-six fields. For both outside parity signs, the three uniform sextic equations have 17 monomials and exact Buchberger reduction reaches the unit ideal in both fields, after 57 S-pairs for delta=-1 and 55 for delta=+1. Thus the final two S1 cells in this row are empty, all ten representative-row S1 cells are deleted, and the accepted four-row frontier falls from 72 to 70.",
